ath9k: add extended 5GHz channels and raise default max_power

Add channels 144, 169, 173, 177, 181 (5720-5905 MHz) to the
5GHz channel table. Raise default max_power from 20 to 30 dBm.
Update ATH9K_NUM_CHANNELS to match new channel count.

The ar9344 synthesizer can tune to these frequencies. Actual
usability depends on regulatory domain and EEPROM calibration.

For research purposes only.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/common-init.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/common-init.c
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@
 	.band = NL80211_BAND_5GHZ, \
 	.center_freq = (_freq), \
 	.hw_value = (_idx), \
-	.max_power = 20, \
+	.max_power = 30, \
 }

 /* Some 2 GHz radios are actually tunable on 2312-2732
@@ -80,12 +80,18 @@
